IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `disc-dates`
IMPORT `disc-claims`

-- Discrimination Act 1991 (ACT) -- worked cases for the questions of the person discriminated against, harassed,
-- vilified or victimised.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the dates and answers used below`

`11 Apr 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 11 4 2025
`12 Apr 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 12 4 2025
`7 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 7 11 2026
`11 Apr 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 11 4 2027
`12 Apr 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 12 4 2027
`28 Feb 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2025
`1 Mar 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2025
`1 Jun 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 2026
`31 Dec 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 12 2026
`1 Jan 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2027
`28 Feb 2028` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2028
`29 Feb 2028` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2028
`1 Mar 2028` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2028
`30 Jun 2030` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 6 2030
`29 Feb 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2024
`27 Feb 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 27 2 2027
`28 Feb 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2027

`PROTECTED` MEANS `yes: a protected attribute under s 7`
`NOT LISTED` MEANS `no: not one of the attributes s 7 (1) lists (the text's no)`
`NOT SHOWN 7` MEANS `not shown: s 7 (2) says what the attribute includes without closing the list (NOTHING-kind)`

`DIRECT` MEANS `direct discrimination (s 8 (2))`
`INDIRECT` MEANS `indirect discrimination (s 8 (3))`
`BOTH` MEANS `direct and indirect discrimination (s 8 (2), (3))`
`REASONABLE CONDITION` MEANS `no discrimination: the condition is reasonable in the circumstances (s 8 (4)) (the text's no)`
`NO DISCRIMINATION` MEANS `no discrimination under s 8 (the text's no)`

`COVERED` MEANS `covered: Part 3 makes discrimination in this area, by this act, unlawful (unless an exception or exemption applies)`
`23C EXCLUDED` MEANS `not covered: s 23C (2) takes this act of a public authority outside s 23C (the text's no)`
`NOT COVERED` MEANS `not covered: Part 3 does not reach this area or this act (NOTHING-kind)`

`job seeker` MEANS `s 10 (1): an employer, when I sought employment`
`employee` MEANS `s 10 (2): my employer, while I am or was employed`
`school` MEANS `s 18: an educational authority`
`shop` MEANS `s 20: a provider of goods, services or facilities`
`public authority` MEANS `s 23C: a public authority administering a territory law or an ACT government program or policy`
`private setting` MEANS `none of these areas`

`UNLAWFUL` MEANS `unlawful discrimination: you may complain to the Human Rights Commission (this Act itself gives no right to sue, s 72, and it is not an offence, s 71)`
`NOT S 8` MEANS `not unlawful: what was done is not discrimination under s 8 (the text's no)`
`NOT S 23C` MEANS `not unlawful: s 23C (2) takes this act of a public authority outside Part 3 (the text's no)`
`OUTSIDE PART 3` MEANS `not shown: Part 3 does not reach this area or this act (NOTHING-kind)`
`S 30` MEANS `not unlawful: it was done necessarily to comply with a territory law, a determination or direction under one, or a court or ACAT order (s 30) (the text's no)`
`EXCEPTION` MEANS `not unlawful: the other side has established a Part 4 exception (the text's no)`
`EXEMPTION` MEANS `not unlawful: the other side holds an exemption from the Human Rights Commission under s 109 (the text's no)`

`DATA DONE` MEANS `done: the insurer or fund has given you the access s 28 (3) requires`
`DATA OWED` MEANS `still owed: the insurer or fund must give you a copy, a written explanation, or inspection (s 28 (3)); the Act sets no deadline`
`DATA NOT ASKED` MEANS `no duty yet: s 28 (3) arises only when you ask for access to the data or documents (the text's no)`

`advance` MEANS `an unwelcome sexual advance`
`request` MEANS `an unwelcome request for sexual favours`
`statement` MEANS `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature, including a sexual statement to me or in my presence, spoken or written`
`HARASSED` MEANS `unlawful sexual harassment: you may complain to the Human Rights Commission`
`NOT HARASSMENT` MEANS `not unlawful: what happened is not sexual harassment under s 58 (the text's no)`
`NOT PART 5` MEANS `not shown: Part 5 does not reach sexual harassment by this person in this setting (NOTHING-kind)`

`VILIFIED` MEANS `unlawful vilification: you may complain to the Human Rights Commission (serious vilification is also an offence, Criminal Code s 750)`
`67A DEFENCE` MEANS `not unlawful: s 67A (2) says this is not unlawful (the text's no)`
`NOT 67A` MEANS `not shown: s 67A (1) does not reach it -- another ground, in private, or not inciting hatred, revulsion, serious contempt or severe ridicule (NOTHING-kind)`

`VICTIMISED` MEANS `unlawful victimisation: you may complain to the Human Rights Commission`
`FALSE CLAIM` MEANS `not victimisation: a claim that is false and not made honestly is not discrimination action (s 68 (2) (h)) (the text's no)`
`NOT 68` MEANS `not shown: s 68 does not reach it -- no detriment or threat, no discrimination action, or not because of it (NOTHING-kind)`
`a complaint` MEANS `making a discrimination complaint to the Human Rights Commission`
`a claim` MEANS `claiming that someone did an unlawful act or committed serious vilification`

`AD UNLAWFUL` MEANS `unlawful advertising (s 69): you may complain to the Human Rights Commission`
`AD NOT SHOWN` MEANS `not shown: s 69 does not reach an advertisement that does not indicate such an intention (NOTHING-kind)`

`ANSWERABLE` MEANS `yes: the employer or principal is taken to have done it too (s 121A (2))`
`REASONABLE STEPS` MEANS `no: they took all reasonable steps to prevent it (s 121A (3)) (the text's no)`
`OUTSIDE AUTHORITY` MEANS `no: the conduct was not by their employee or agent within the scope of their authority (s 121A (2)) (the text's no)`

`ADJ UNLAWFUL` MEANS `unlawful: failing to make reasonable adjustments for you is an unlawful act (s 74 (3))`
`ADJ MADE` MEANS `no breach: they made reasonable adjustments for your needs`
`ADJ HARDSHIP` MEANS `no breach: the adjustment would cause them unjustifiable hardship, so it is not a reasonable adjustment (s 74 (2)) (the text's no)`
`ADJ NO DUTY` MEANS `no duty: discrimination on that ground is not unlawful here -- outside Part 3, or an exception or exemption applies (ss 74 (1), 76) (the text's no)`
`ADJ NO NEED` MEANS `no duty: you have no particular need arising from a protected attribute (s 74 (1)) (the text's no)`

`government body` MEANS `an ACT government directorate, territory authority or territory instrumentality`
`government manager` MEANS `an individual who controls or directs one of those`
`any business` MEANS `any other organisation or business, or an individual who controls or directs one`
`DUTY APPLIES` MEANS `yes: they must take reasonable and proportionate steps to eliminate the discrimination, sexual harassment and vilification (s 75 (2))`
`DUTY NOT YET` MEANS `not yet: s 75 (4) puts off the duty for them until a later day (the text's no)`
`DUTY NOT BOUND` MEANS `no: s 75 applies only to an organisation, business or manager required by the Act not to discriminate, harass or vilify in the circumstances (s 75 (1)) (the text's no)`
`DUTY EXCEPTED` MEANS `no: a Part 4 exception or a Part 10 exemption applies (s 76) (the text's no)`

§ `Dates module`

-- 29 February 2024 plus 3 years is 28 February 2027 (no 29 February in 2027); plus 4 years is 29 February 2028.
#ASSERT DATE_SERIAL (`29 Feb 2024` `plus years` 3) EQUALS DATE_SERIAL `28 Feb 2027`
#ASSERT DATE_SERIAL (`29 Feb 2024` `plus years` 4) EQUALS DATE_SERIAL `29 Feb 2028`
#ASSERT DATE_SERIAL (`1 Mar 2025` `plus years` 3) EQUALS DATE_SERIAL `1 Mar 2028`
#ASSERT `is a leap year` 2000
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a leap year` 1900))

§ `s 7 -- protected attributes`

#ASSERT `s 7 -- is the ground a protected attribute` `race` `I have it` EQUALS `PROTECTED`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- is the ground a protected attribute` `age` `I am thought to have had it in the past` EQUALS `PROTECTED`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- is the ground a protected attribute` `disability` `it is a characteristic people with the attribute are generally presumed to have` EQUALS `PROTECTED`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- is the ground a protected attribute` `some other attribute` `I have it` EQUALS `NOT LISTED`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- is the ground a protected attribute` `sex` `none of these links` EQUALS `NOT SHOWN 7`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- is the ground a protected attribute` `some other attribute` `none of these links` EQUALS `NOT LISTED`

§ `Dictionary -- irrelevant criminal record`

#ASSERT `dictionary -- is my record an irrelevant criminal record` `charged, and the proceeding is not finalised` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `dictionary -- is my record an irrelevant criminal record` `acquitted` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `dictionary -- is my record an irrelevant criminal record` `served with an infringement notice for it` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`dictionary -- is my record an irrelevant criminal record` `convicted, and the conviction is not spent or extinguished` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `dictionary -- is my record an irrelevant criminal record` `convicted, and the conviction is not spent or extinguished` FALSE FALSE
-- A spent conviction: relevant and s 16 does not apply -> not irrelevant; relevant and s 16 applies -> irrelevant.
#ASSERT (NOT (`dictionary -- is my record an irrelevant criminal record` `convicted, and the conviction is spent under the Spent Convictions Act 2000` TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `dictionary -- is my record an irrelevant criminal record` `convicted, and the conviction is spent under the Spent Convictions Act 2000` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `dictionary -- is my record an irrelevant criminal record` `convicted, and the conviction is spent under the Spent Convictions Act 2000` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `dictionary -- is my record an irrelevant criminal record` `convicted, and the conviction is extinguished under the Spent Convictions Act 2000` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`dictionary -- is my record an irrelevant criminal record` `none of these records` FALSE FALSE))

§ `s 8 -- direct and indirect discrimination`

#ASSERT `s 8 -- was I discriminated against` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `DIRECT`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- was I discriminated against` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `INDIRECT`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- was I discriminated against` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `BOTH`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- was I discriminated against` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `REASONABLE CONDITION`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- was I discriminated against` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `DIRECT`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- was I discriminated against` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NO DISCRIMINATION`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- was I discriminated against` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NO DISCRIMINATION`

§ `Part 3 -- the areas`

#ASSERT `Part 3 -- does the Act cover where I was discriminated against` `employee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `COVERED`
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- does the Act cover where I was discriminated against` `shop` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT COVERED`
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- does the Act cover where I was discriminated against` `private setting` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT COVERED`
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- does the Act cover where I was discriminated against` `public authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `23C EXCLUDED`
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- does the Act cover where I was discriminated against` `public authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `COVERED`
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- does the Act cover where I was discriminated against` `shop` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `COVERED`

#ASSERT `s 11 -- may my employer refuse my religious practice at work` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `unlawful: refusing permission for this religious practice in working hours is discrimination under s 11`
#ASSERT `s 11 -- may my employer refuse my religious practice at work` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not shown under s 11: the practice does not meet the conditions s 11 sets (s 10 (2) may still apply) (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 11 -- may my employer refuse my religious practice at work` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not shown under s 11: the practice does not meet the conditions s 11 sets (s 10 (2) may still apply) (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `Part 4 -- the exceptions screen`

-- A job applicant refused on age: ss 24, 25, 27, 30, 32, 33B, 33C, 57B, 57C, 57G (worked through the 42 exceptions).
#ASSERT `Part 4 -- which exceptions could the other side rely on` `job seeker` `age` EQUALS LIST `s 24 domestic duties in the employer's home`, `s 25 residential care of children`, `s 27 measures intended to achieve equality`, `s 30 acts done necessarily to comply with a territory law or an order`, `s 32 religious bodies`, `s 33B genuine occupational qualifications`, `s 33C inherent requirements of employment`, `s 57B youth wages`, `s 57C health and safety at work (age)`, `s 57G legal incapacity because of age`
-- A shop refusing service on disability: ss 27, 28, 30, 31, 32, 33A, 53, 56.
#ASSERT `Part 4 -- which exceptions could the other side rely on` `shop` `disability` EQUALS LIST `s 27 measures intended to achieve equality`, `s 28 insurance and superannuation`, `s 30 acts done necessarily to comply with a territory law or an order`, `s 31 clubs and voluntary bodies for people sharing an attribute`, `s 32 religious bodies`, `s 33A charging for accommodation, goods or services`, `s 53 goods and services provided in a special way`, `s 56 public health`
-- A school on religious conviction: ss 27, 30, 32, 46.
#ASSERT `Part 4 -- which exceptions could the other side rely on` `school` `religious conviction` EQUALS LIST `s 27 measures intended to achieve equality`, `s 30 acts done necessarily to comply with a territory law or an order`, `s 32 religious bodies`, `s 46 religious educational institutions`
-- An employee on religious conviction: s 33B is closed to that ground (s 33B (2)); s 44 does not name s 10 (2).
#ASSERT `Part 4 -- which exceptions could the other side rely on` `employee` `religious conviction` EQUALS LIST `s 27 measures intended to achieve equality`, `s 30 acts done necessarily to comply with a territory law or an order`, `s 32 religious bodies`, `s 46 religious educational institutions`
-- Outside Part 3: no exception is needed or listed.
#ASSERT null (`Part 4 -- which exceptions could the other side rely on` `private setting` `sex`)

